(footprint "SOT-353_SC-70-5_Slim"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(layer "B.Cu")
	(descr "SOT-353 / SC-70-5, AS-BUILT PolyKybd land pattern - pads 0.65 x 0.40 at x +/-0.95. EXTRACTED FROM THE BOARD deliberately, and named _Slim so it can never be confused with the stock KiCad footprint. WHY: KiCad's Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-353_SC-70-5 has since been REDRAWN to 1.025 x 0.35 roundrect at x +/-0.8375 - the pad is 58% longer and the growth is almost entirely at the HEEL (inner edge 0.625 -> 0.325), which closes the gap between the two pad columns from 1.25 mm to 0.65 mm and runs straight through the corridor where traces pass under the package. Adopting it was measured at 189 real trace overlaps across the four boards, hitting every one of the 14 buffers on every board, in exchange for heel land that sits under the body where it cannot be inspected anyway (the toe gains only 0.075 mm, and the pad gets NARROWER, 0.40 -> 0.35). So the as-built land is kept. Verified identical across all 54 instances on split72 left/right and split42 left/right. Lead per Nexperia SOT353-1: bp 0.15-0.30, Lp 0.26-0.46, HE 1.8-2.4, pitch 0.65 - giving a toe fillet of +0.225 mm nominal and +0.075 mm at max span. Do NOT 'update from library' without re-running DRC.")
	(tags "SOT-353 SC-70-5 TSSOP5 as-built slim")
